Close other files or all files from a file tab's right-click menu.

Right-click a file tab in the workspace rail for Close, Close other files
and Close all files. Closing the active file activates its nearest
remaining neighbour, as the tab's x does, and closing them all goes back to
the scope view (the Changed or All list). Only file tabs close:
shells, browsers and side chats stay open, since closing a shell kills it.
Close other files is greyed out when only one file is open.

AppShell's closeFile becomes closeFiles, which closes a list of tabs, and
closeFile calls it with one.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0044.

